# Shared Components

Uniform, reusable UI built on Flutter Material primitives.

## Requirements

- Prefer Material/Cupertino widgets; wrap only for consistency or repeated behavior.
- Reusable components must live under `frontend/lib/shared/`; must not duplicate in feature folders, and check the catalog before creating new UI.
- Must not create multiple components for one job or embed product business logic.
- Optimize for performance: `const` constructors, focused rebuilds, lazy builders for large lists.
- Match design tokens on every variant ([`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc)) and adapt to mobile, tablet, desktop ([`layouts.mdc`](./layouts.mdc)).
- All labels, hints, validation, and accessibility text must be localized.
- Support enabled, disabled, loading, error, focused, and empty states where relevant.
- Data-bound components render Riverpod changes immediately without owning sync logic.
- Reference entities by `human_friendly_id`; must not expose raw table IDs.
- Enforce RBAC+ABAC: unauthorized menus, components, and actions must not render ([`permissions.mdc`](./permissions.mdc)).
- Module work-queue screens must follow [`ui-workspace.mdc`](./ui-workspace.mdc).

## Standard catalog

Reuse the standard set instead of new abstractions: `AppWorkspace`, `AppListTable`, `AppWorkspaceDetailPanel`, `AppActionPanel`, `AppPermissionActionPanel`, `AppWorkspaceMutationDialog`, `AppButton`, `AppTextField`, `AppSelectField`, `AppRadioGroup`, `AppCheckboxField`, `AppSwitchField`, `AppDateField`, `AppDialog`, `AsyncStateScaffold`, `AppStatusBadge`, `ResponsivePage`, `ResponsiveAppShell`, `SideNavigation`.

Detail modal and workspace titled sections use `AppWorkspaceDetailPanel` (collapsible by default; see [`ui-workspace.mdc`](./ui-workspace.mdc)). Adapters: titled `AppSectionPanel`, framed `AppFormSection`, `AppScreenSection`, and `AppExpandableRecordSection`. Do not invent feature-local section chrome.

## Styling bounds

- Icons `20–24px`; button heights `40–48px`.
- Radii from `theme.radius` tokens via `context.responsiveRadius(...)`.
- Form fields expose validation hooks but must not own feature rules.

